BioSQA Studio — model weights: provenance and inherited terms
=============================================================

The MIT License in `LICENSE` covers the **source code** of BioSQA Studio.

It does **not** grant any rights over the trained model weights shipped in
`models/` (`ecg.onnx`, `ppg.onnx`, `eeg.onnx`, `eda.onnx`). Those files are
derived from third-party biosignal datasets, and each dataset carries its own
access and use terms. Some of those terms are restrictive: credentialed access
with a signed data use agreement (MIMIC-III derivatives, TUH/TUAR), or
research/non-commercial use only (WESAD).

This file records, per shipped model, which datasets it was trained on and what
those sources require. It is a **provenance statement, not legal advice and not
a compliance certificate** — the terms below are summarised from the dataset
providers' own published conditions and have not been reviewed by a lawyer. If
you intend to redistribute these weights, embed them in a product, or use them
commercially, check each source's current terms yourself, or retrain on sources
whose terms you have verified.

The same information is available machine-readably in the `license` block of
each `models/<modality>.model_card.json`.

No dataset itself is redistributed with this app.


ecg.onnx  (v3-dualbranch-spectral)
----------------------------------
Trained on the ECG corpus of `store_v2`, plus synthetic artifact augmentation:

  PhysioNet/CinC Challenge 2011, BUT QDB, European ST-T Database,
  MIT-BIH Malignant Ventricular Ectopy DB (VFDB), MIT-BIH Noise Stress Test DB
  (NSTDB), MIT-BIH Supraventricular Arrhythmia DB (SVDB), PTB-XL.

All are open-access PhysioNet datasets (Open Data Commons Attribution / CC BY
family). Redistribution: **attribution-required**, no access restriction known.
Carry the citations in `README.md` § Datasets forward.


ppg.onnx  (v4-4cohort-dalia-ordlogit)
-------------------------------------
Trained on the PPG corpus of `store_ppg4_tmb` — four cohorts, verified against
that store's segment index:

  BUT PPG                open access (PhysioNet)
  MIMIC-III-Ext-PPG      RESTRICTED — PhysioNet credentialed access; requires
                         completed training and a signed data use agreement
                         (MIMIC-III derivative)
  PPG-DaLiA              open access (UCI ML Repository, CC BY)
  WESAD (wrist PPG)      RESTRICTED — research use; the dataset's own terms
                         exclude commercial use

Redistribution: **restricted**. These weights are derived in part from a
credentialed dataset and from a dataset licensed for non-commercial research
use. Do not treat the MIT code licence as covering them. Commercial use is not
supported by the upstream terms.


eda.onnx  (v3-combined-fusion-ordlogit)
---------------------------------------
Trained on the EDA corpus of `store_v3` — three cohorts, verified against that
store's segment index:

  EDABE                              research use (Zenodo release)
  EDA-Artifact-Detection (UT Dallas)  research use
  EDA-Artifact-Detection (Alan Walks Wales)  research use

Redistribution: **review-required**. All three are openly downloadable research
datasets, but none of their terms has been individually verified as permitting
redistribution of derived model weights. (Note: WESAD EDA is part of the wider
research corpus but is *not* in this shipped model's training store.)


eeg.onnx  (v5-multihead-expert-grade-cleaned)
---------------------------------------------
Trained on the EEG corpus of `store_v8`:

  TUAR (TUH EEG Artifact Corpus)   RESTRICTED — requires a signed Temple
                                   University data use agreement; the data may
                                   not be redistributed
  PhysioMotion (ds006386)          CC0 (OpenNeuro)
  Phantom-EEG (ds004784)           CC0 (OpenNeuro)
  Mind-in-Motion (ds004625)        CC0 (OpenNeuro)
  Motion-Artifact fNIRS+EEG        open access (PhysioNet)

The grade and usable heads were trained on TUAR + PhysioMotion only; the
artifact-type head uses all five cohorts. Either way TUAR is in the lineage.

Redistribution: **restricted**. The Temple DUA governs the data; it does not
grant terms for derived weights, so redistribution of this model has not been
established as permitted.


If you need unrestricted weights
--------------------------------
Retrain on the open-access cohorts only (the ECG lineage is already in that
category) and re-export with `reproducibility/scripts/export_*.py`. The
architecture, training loop and export path are all in `reproducibility/`.
